  "ruled": [
    "THE DRAWING’S SIZE (the owner, 10-28, “Bigger, with field marks”, made in pass E): each species with a def is drawn for its plate by its own rig’s renderPlate, in a 160 × 96 cell, filling the frame at about 3x the game’s sprite, with the marks a field guide shows (plates.<id>.marks): the game’s colours and shape at the page’s pixel size, never a new fish. The game’s sprites are unchanged.",
    "THE CLAM (the owner, 10-28): a plate-size clam drawing in Shellfish2, which the plate draws: Shellfish2.renderPlate (pass D; a 160 × 96 cell since pass E), side-on with its siphon, at P / 32 like every other species. Its siphon stays as drawn (pass D’s question 4).",
    "THE LOBSTER (the owner, 10-28, “Olive in pass E”): Crustacean2 draws the live lobster dark olive, and so its plate, drawn once; red is kept for a cooked one.",
    "THE WORDS (the owner, 10-28): the player’s words on a plate come from the game’s writers, through the coordinator; the team notes stay cut, and nothing is invented. Until they come the plate prints the def’s words: the enums’ names with no labels, and two lines in the team’s words for the game (“the trap-arc’s”, “the St Peters opening’s”), which print until the writers’ words come (pass D’s question 6).",
    "THE FURNITURE (the owner, 10-28): the bar’s label is the caption; the running head and the tabs stay the Notebook’s; the plate’s page scale stands."
  ]
